  {
   "id": 19,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    40,
    880
   ],
   "size": [
    670,
    620
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 19,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "How to use",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Anima Reference Adapter\n\nTakes the **character and drawing style** from the reference image; **pose, background and framing** come from the prompt.\n\n- **Prompt**: no character name, artist tag or appearance/outfit tags. Write quality tags, gender, `solo` and scene tags (framing, pose, expression, background, lighting). Adding a few appearance tags is fine.\n- **Anima Ref Latent**: fits the reference into the output size (aspect kept, white padding). The output size is set here (it also returns the empty latent).\n- **Anima Ref Guider**\n  - `cfg`: text guidance (4.5)\n  - `ref_guidance`: reference guidance. 1 = reference in both CFG branches (weak); 4.5-6 recommended. Higher gives more character detail and style, and more saturation.\n  - `correction`: `apg` (default) or `rescale` (phi 0.5) tames over-saturation at high guidance.\n- **Anima Ref Adapter Loader**: the adapter LoRA. Keep `ref_offset_h` at 1.0 (training value).\n- Base: Anima base v1.0 without the turbo LoRA (the adapter was trained on the base model), bf16 compute, SageAttention, euler 30 steps.\n- With ref_guidance != 1 each step runs the model 3 times (1.5x a normal CFG step).\n\nThis is a pilot adapter (300 characters, 2,000 steps): small patterns, scars and skin tones are weak.\n\n### PAG\n- **Anima Safe PAG** adds detail from the difference to a prediction with block 18 self-attention blurred (scale 1.3, 0.3-0.8 of the schedule). One extra model call per step while active.\n- **Avoid SamplerSPEED for now**: its half-resolution stage needs a half-size reference, which this adapter never saw in training; results are unreliable.\n"
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
